course: dictionary
lesson: 1463
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. The dictionary gives cast seven meanings. «The cast takes a bow at the end of the school play.» The clue is school play, so cast means the actors in the show.
explain: «The doctor put a cast on her broken arm.» The clues are doctor and broken arm, so a cast here is a hard cover that keeps a bone still while it heals. «The tree cast a long shadow across the grass» means the tree made a shadow fall on the grass. The word shadow tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Try this with «She cast her vote for the class captain»: to cast a vote means to put your choice in, so it fits.
fact: Cast can be a verb (to throw, to give a part, to make an object) or a noun (a hard cover, or all the actors in a show).
fact: «Cast» means to throw something, such as a fishing line or a net.
fact: A cast is a hard covering, often of plaster, that protects a broken arm or leg while it heals.
fact: «Cast» also means all the actors in a play, film or show.
fact: Phrases to know: cast a shadow, cast a spell, cast a vote, cast off, cast out.
exercise: «The cast of the school play took a bow.» What does cast mean here? | A hard cover for a broken arm | *All the actors in the play | To throw something into the sea | To make a shadow fall
exercise: «The tree cast a long shadow across the grass.» What does cast mean here? | To pour hot metal into a mould | *To make a shadow fall | To throw a net | To give someone a part in a film
exercise: After Sam broke his leg, the doctor put a cast on it. What is a cast here? | A magic spell | A group of actors | *A hard cover that stops the bone moving while it heals | A fishing rod
test: «She cast her vote for the class captain.» What does cast mean here? | A hard shell of plaster | To give someone a part in a play | To throw a fishing line | *To put in a vote, choosing someone
test: «Many dinosaur skeletons in museums are casts, copies made from moulds.» What is a cast here? | A group of actors | *A copy made from a mould | A real fossil bone | A hard cover for a broken bone
exam: Which meaning of cast fits «Some stable ankle breaks heal well in a removable boot instead of a cast»? | A fishing net | *A hard cover that holds a broken bone still | The actors in a film | A spell cast by a wizard
